      "resource_type": "story",
      "text": "Wave 1 source review for Wave 3 ownership — actionable MiniApps exact-UTF8 seam at CURRENT App commit 9f0cbdffbda45520124ee1f0b50961641c5c49b1 / tree dbe46fdd4128843bb3bb687bd00ae69d024f12b5 (read-only HEAD re-observed, no app edits).\n\nIn Modules/PinkhaAnyUI/Sources/PinkhaAnyUI/AnyMiniAppsResultApplier.swift, SHA256 057bf2f049572306171c9980876222fd6e8196f5fb82aa7c66bfe2420a9f8cc2 (16,018 bytes), the replay/readback checks still use synthesized metadata/String equality: actual!=before/expected (line42), actual==before/expected (64/84), metadata==expected (81), intent.text==text (145), block.text==intent.text (158), and file metadata strings (230–232). Swift canonical String equality is not exact UTF8 identity. The newly published Engine/Host exact-value comparator does not automatically change these caller checks. Heart MiniApps result text uses its own String comparison too. Please keep any correction in the owning consumer lane and add only focused composed/decomposed text/name controls; do not globally redefine AnyJSON or replay native network proofs.\n\nExisting Any ownership is concrete: mounted document→performMiniAppsMutation/nativeSession lease, original client/workspace, conditional document edits, prepared native plans/source keys, local journal before bridge ACK. This review did not find an additional absent native storage/ACL/sync primitive. It is a caller verification seam, not evidence that an old or new engine bypasses ACL.\n\nSeparate UNPROVEN check: file name/MIME are compared to input hints, but this caller uses PREPARED inline/full APIs. Ordinary streaming-upload normalization evidence cannot be applied to that path by inference. Join the exact prepared implementation before treating normalization/omission as a defect; retain original prepared identity and uncertainty without resend.\n\nPublic readback SHA3b57bb67… binds all four reviewed files. Independent C review is local migration-relay/miniapps-app9f0-source-review.md SHA58235